James sought advice on organizing a recommendation letter for his PhD student, Mohammad Taky Tahmid, focusing on his postdoctoral project proposal about heat exposure and productivity in Bangladesh rice mills. I suggested positioning the project description early in the letter to establish credibility and relevance. The recommended structure included an initial endorsement, the project overview, evidence of Tahmid’s capabilities through past research accomplishments, dissertation highlights, and a final note on collegiality and service. I emphasized matching the letter's content to the committee's interests in climate adaptation and labor productivity. A revised opening was also suggested to clarify Tahmid’s current academic status and background. The approach aims to clearly demonstrate Tahmid's qualifications and the project's importance.

